# Not committed, and not an oversight. Hypothesis keys stored examples on a
# digest over the test function's own source, so an entry is orphaned by the
# first edit to the test and carries nothing between checkouts. Committing this
# would look like counterexamples travel when they do not. They travel as
# `@example` -- see AGENTS.md.
.hypothesis/
htmlcov/

# An audit report quotes the answer it audited, and the answer quotes the
# corpus. A report committed by accident publishes both. See
# docs/threat-model.md once it exists; until then, treat every *.audit.json
# as if it were the notes themselves.
*.audit.json
reports/
